course: dictionary
lesson: 15499
title: Stunting: growing, slowing and stunts
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word stunting has three meanings, so check the words around it. Context tells you which one is meant. «Poor food when she was very young led to stunting, so she is shorter than most children her age.» Here stunting means not growing as tall as you should.
explain: As a verb form of stunt, stunting means slowing or stopping growth. «Dry soil is stunting the young tomato plants.» The plants are not growing as well as they should, and the soil is the cause.
explain: Stunting can also mean doing stunts, which are daring tricks. «The rider was stunting on his bike, spinning high off the ramp.» The words bike, ramp and spinning are the clues. Ask: what would fit here? A trick fits, not growth.
fact: Stunting (noun) means not growing as tall or as well as you should.
fact: Health workers often talk about child stunting when children did not get enough good food when they were very young.
fact: In plant experiments, poor light or poor soil can cause stunting.
fact: «Stunting» can also mean doing daring tricks on bikes, skateboards, cars or planes.
fact: Check the clues: words about food, light or height point to growth; words about jumps, spins or ramps point to tricks.
exercise: «Poor light is stunting the seedlings.» What does stunting mean here? | Doing tricks on a bike | Watering them too much | Painting the leaves bright green | *Slowing or stopping growth
exercise: «The skateboarder was stunting down the ramp, spinning in the air.» What does stunting mean here? | Growing taller every day | Being very quiet | Sleeping in the sun | *Doing daring tricks
exercise: Health workers talk about child stunting. What does this usually describe? | Children who are very tall for their age | Children who like doing tricks on bikes | Children who have new shoes | *Children who are shorter than they should be, often after too little good food when very young
test: «Lack of water is stunting the young oak tree.» Which meaning of stunting fits best? | Making a loud noise | Doing stunts in a film | Winning a race | *Stopping or slowing its growth
test: «The pilot was stunting over the sea, flying in loops.» What does stunting mean? | Hiding from the wind | *Doing daring tricks in the air | Stopping the engine | Growing as tall as a tree
exam: Which sentence uses stunting to mean not growing as well as it should? | The stunting show is on at the cinema tonight. | The cat was stunting across the garden fence. | *«Poor food and illness are stunting the growth of some children in the village.» | Lots of children in the club love stunting on their scooters.
